WEBVTT

00:04:29.958 --> 00:04:31.934
After her six years of being underpaid,

00:04:31.958 --> 00:04:33.851
Grace finally asked for a raise,

00:04:33.875 --> 00:04:36.375
but she left it to her boss
to make the first offer.

00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:41.268
If you're like most people, you believe
that's the way to get the best results.

00:04:41.292 --> 00:04:44.684
You don't want to tip your hand
before you see the other person's cards,

00:04:44.708 --> 00:04:47.018
but the evidence suggests that's backward.

00:04:47.042 --> 00:04:49.559
(Upbeat music)

00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:51.643
First offers serve as anchors.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:53.601
They set the hook for the negotiation,

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:55.292
and it's hard to escape the pull.

00:04:56.583 --> 00:04:59.934
One comprehensive analysis
of negotiation experiment showed

00:04:59.958 --> 00:05:02.393
that every dollar higher
in the first offer